## Reference anatomy atlases

`bun run anatomy:fetch` downloads three model files into the gitignored `data/anatomy/`. They are not part of this repository and are licensed separately (CC BY 4.0); the viewer shows their credits whenever they are displayed:

- BodyParts3D, © The Database Center for Life Science licensed under CC Attribution 4.0 International. (DBCLS's written confirmation of the 2025 relicence from CC BY-SA 2.1 JP is still pending.)
- 3D anatomical structures from the HuBMAP Human Reference Atlas (HRA), humanatlas.io, CC BY 4.0.

The files were merged, simplified and shaded (ambient occlusion) by the Open Science Foundation's open-twin-xr; TwinLLM only positions them. Pins and details: `docs/anatomy.md`.

## Synthetic demo bodies

`bun run anatomy:fetch` also downloads two synthetic demo bodies into the gitignored `data/anatomy/`. They are not part of this repository and are licensed separately (Apache-2.0 code over CC0-1.0 shape assets); the viewer shows this credit whenever the demo body is displayed:

- ANNY, a free-to-use 3D human parametric model for all ages — NAVER LABS Europe / NAVER Corporation. Apache-2.0 code over CC0 shape assets derived from MakeHuman. Cite arXiv:2511.03589. Baked to static geometry by this repository; no scan of any person was used.

"This repository" in that credit is the Open Science Foundation's open-twin-xr, which baked and posed the bodies; TwinLLM only positions them. Pins and details: `docs/anatomy.md`.

`bun run anatomy:bake-rigged` bakes rigged variants of the same two bodies locally, with ANNY's skeleton and skin weights, from the `anny` Python package (same licences). They are not part of this repository either; the viewer then shows this credit:

- ANNY, a free-to-use 3D human parametric model for all ages — NAVER LABS Europe / NAVER Corporation. Apache-2.0 code over CC0 shape assets derived from MakeHuman. Cite arXiv:2511.03589. Baked with its skeleton by this repository; no scan of any person was used.

Here "this repository" is TwinLLM (`scripts/anatomy/bake-anny-rigged.py`). The walk, run, idle and dance-loop clips use no motion-capture data.

`python/motion/fetch_model.py` downloads the MediaPipe Pose Landmarker model (Google, Apache-2.0) into the gitignored `data/motion/models/` for making motion clips from a video locally. It is not part of this repository, and neither is any clip made with it.

